  "description": "EEG recordings from 8 healthy participants performing self-initiated, self-paced reaching movements under two conditions: unilateral (right arm) and bilateral (both arms). Data were recorded with a 64-channel wireless active-electrode system at 500 Hz across six runs per subject. The dataset supports movement intention recognition for exoskeleton-supported stroke rehabilitation and is distributed in BIDS format via MOABB.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with a Brain Products LiveAmp64 (64 active Acticap slim electrodes, extended 10-20 montage, reference FCz, ground AFz) at 500 Hz with hardware prefiltering of 0.1-131 Hz. Participants performed 3 sets of 40 self-initiated movements per condition (unilateral right arm button press, bilateral synchronous arm movement), one run per set.",
